        "client_msg_id": "7664572a-67b5-4f71-9f21-39cc77b9397d",
        "text": "<@U03FEH3N8> I summed up your statements about the questionnaire, here are my answers and comments.\nEducation \/ work \/ status ok\n\n\nReligion: deleted\nnationality\/substance concerns\n\nNationality gives information about residential area\nSubstance use --&gt; influences brain activity in general, in particular the brain works different in addicts\n\n“If we were setting up an experiment in academia, an ethic committee would refuse it as the rule is “only get information that’s going to be used” ... like substance used is very intrusive”\n--&gt; see above + every information can be used. In this case, it would serve as exclusion criteria.\n\n“would it not be better to have a little questionnaire with travel related question : how often do you go in holidays ? outside or within the country ? alone, with someone, with a group of friend, with an organization or you organize it yourself”\n--&gt; This actually does not interest me, in particular as it is qualitative data noone will ever analyse :wink:. The questions created are rather generic and will serve the purpose for general description of experimental research groups",
